Facing the problem where I need to build the same codebase for a nordic uC and an stm32f4 uC.

Even though this was merged in recently

https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/pull/20657/files#diff-722b2739b6d0b69a16ee867da52074d6R58

Looks like for stm32 targets, pwm flag usage is not supported

https://github.com/vestas-wind-systems/zephyr/blob/162a49d963f0b9b94c3e25ef8de75f89f7fb4a71/drivers/pwm/pwm_stm32.c#L87-L90

One could #ifdef the application code to provide 1-period as value for the PWM signal. But Since the mechanism is there, would be nice to harmonize usage across targets.

@erwango 
@rsalveti 
@idlethread
Is there any plans to support this for stm?
